# data/ holds everything large and regenerable. Each subfolder is listed
# individually rather than ignoring data/ wholesale, so that the list itself
# documents what belongs there -- and so anything small dropped directly in
# data/ (a note, a manifest) still gets tracked. Add a line here when a new
# large artefact appears; see README "Where things live".

# Trajectory CSVs (~17GB) -- regenerate via notebooks/00_make_dataset.ipynb
data/square_room_100steps_2.2m_1000000/

# Converted training shards (~2.3GB) -- regenerate via notebooks/01_prepare_data.ipynb
data/shards/

# Model weights. Supervised runs (~45MB, notebooks/02_train.ipynb) are small;
# RL runs (train_rl_agent.py) are not -- a single full checkpoint (weights +
# optimizer + both replay buffers) is ~19.7GB, and only the most recent one is
# worth keeping (see README "RL agent").
data/checkpoints/

# results/ is the opposite: small, kept, and tracked. Figures only.

# Run logs
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Editor config -- recommends an extension, not needed to run anything
.vscode/
